# Unicode CLDR, locale ta, dateFields.json, field month.
# A counted noun is CASE-MARKED in Tamil, not bare: the ago pattern is
# the DATIVE unit plus முன், and the in-N pattern is the LOCATIVE on
# the unit with no preposition at all.  Both case forms are unit
# surfaces in their own right, and both are CLDR's own wording.
# மாதம் is the month unit.  திங்கள் also means "month", and is not
# shipped here: it is Monday first and the collision is unresolvable
# inside a phrase, so the unit reading of that word is refused.
மாதம்
மாதங்கள்
மாதத்துக்கு
மாதங்களுக்கு
